SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Magnuson-Stevens Fishery Conservation and Man
 agement Act Provisions\; Fisheries of the Northeastern United States\; Fra
 mework Adjustment 7 to the Atlantic Spiny Dogfish Fishery Management Plan
DESCRIPTION:NMFS proposes measures included in Framework Adjustment 7 to t
 he Spiny Dogfish Fishery Management Plan (FMP)\, as recommended by the Mid
 -Atlantic and New England Fishery Management Councils. Framework 7 propose
 s fishing year 2026 and projected 2027 specifications\, which would establ
 ish allowable harvest levels for the spiny dogfish fishery to prevent over
 fishing while enabling optimum yield based on the best scientific informat
 ion available. Framework 7 also proposes changes to the Atlantic spiny dog
 fish accountability measures intended to provide the commercial fishery wi
 th greater flexibility by no longer requiring full payback of annual catch
  limit (ACL) overages when the Atlantic spiny dogfish stock is considered 
 healthy.\nhttps://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/10/13/2026-20863/
 magnuson-stevens-fishery-conservation-and-management-act-provisions-fisher
 ies-of-the-northeastern
