UID:4d65836b588bcad1@role-business-corporate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261008T231904Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attorney General Aaron M. Frey Seeks Court Ap
 proval for Settlements with Ascend\, Citron\, and Mayne Pharma Over Conspi
 racy to Inflate Prices and Limit Competition
DESCRIPTION:FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nContact: Danna Hayes\nDanna.hayes@maine
 .gov\nIf You Bought Certain Generic Prescription Drugs in the United State
 s Between May 2009 and December 2019\, You Could be Eligible for Money\nAU
 GUSTA – Attorney General Aaron M. Frey today joined a coalition of 45 st
 ates and territories seeking court approval of three settlements with Asce
 nd Laboratories\, Citron Pharma and Mayne Pharma to resolve allegations th
 at the generic drug manufacturers engaged in a widespread\, long-running c
 onspiracy to artificially inflate and manipulate prices\, reduce competiti
 on\, and unreasonably restrain trade with regard to numerous generic presc
 ription drugs.\nAscend will pay $400\,000 to the states. Mayne will pay $6
 50\,000. Citron’s settlement only includes non-monetary terms as it has 
 ceased business operations. As part of the settlement\, the companies each
  agreed to meaningful injunctive terms including a series of internal refo
 rms to ensure fair competition and compliance with antitrust laws.\nThese 
 latest settlements come as the States prepare for the first trial to be he
 ld in Hartford\, Connecticut in February 2027.\nThe States previously reac
 hed settlements with Sandoz\, Glenmark\, Lannett\, Bausch\, Apotex\, Herit
 age\, and Heritage’s parent company\, Emcure\, totaling $496.5 million.\
 nIf you purchased a generic prescription drug between May 2009 and Decembe
 r 2019\, you may be eligible for compensation. To determine your eligibili
 ty\, call\n1-866-290-0182\n(Toll-Free)\, email\ninfo@AGGenericDrugs.com\no
 r visit\nwww.AGGenericDrugs.com\n. You can\nsubmit a claim for compensatio
 n\n.\nConnecticut is leading a coalition of nearly all states and territor
 ies engaged in a series of antitrust cases\, starting first in 2016. The f
 irst Complaint included Heritage and 17 other corporate Defendants\, two i
 ndividual Defendants\, and 15 generic drugs. Two former executives from He
 ritage Pharmaceuticals\, Jeffery Glazer and Jason Malek\, have since enter
 ed into settlement agreements and are cooperating. The second \nhttps://ww
 w.maine.gov/ag/news-and-library/press-releases/attorney-general-aaron-m-fr
 ey-seeks-court-approval-settlements
URL:https://www.maine.gov/ag/news-and-library/press-releases/attorney-gene
 ral-aaron-m-frey-seeks-court-approval-settlements
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
