SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Senate Confirms Vaughan Woodruff as Cha
 ir of the State Workforce Development Board
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Maine Senate
  Confirms Vaughan Woodruff as Chair of the State Workforce Development Boa
 rd\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services
 \nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nM
 aine Senate Confirms Vaughan Woodruff as Chair of the State Workforce Deve
 lopment Board\nOctober 5\, 2026\nFor Immediate Release\nMedia Contact: Aut
 umn Mahoney\, Communications Specialist\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA\n- T
 he Maine Senate confirmed Vaughan Woodruff\, principal of EquinoxDG\, to a
  second term as chair of the State Workforce Development Board (SWDB). Gov
 . Janet Mills announced her nomination of Woodruff on Sept. 8\, 2026. Wood
 ruff has served as chair of the SWDB since 2023.\nPrior to founding Equino
 xDG\, Woodruff was vice president of regulatory reform at the Interstate R
 enewable Energy Council and vice president of workforce development and in
 terconnection strategy at ReVision Energy\, where he oversaw the company's
  long-term strategic vision for training and talent development and develo
 ped nationally recognized registered apprenticeships in clean energy.\n"Th
 e State Workforce Development Board plays a critical role in coordinating 
 Maine's workforce development efforts to support economic growth and addre
 ss workforce challenges\," said Maine Department of Labor Commissioner Lau
 ra Fortman. "Vaughan Woodruff is a well-respected business leader with dee
 p workforce expertise. His continued leadership will help maintain momentu
 m as we strengthen Maine's workforce and economy."\n"I appreciate the trus
 t that Gov. Mills and the Maine Senate have placed in me through my nomina
 tion and confirmation to continue serving the people of Maine in this role
 \nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363751
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363751
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
